     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is about double the maximum daily dose, and 1700 mg is well above the maximum single dose. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **You've said you're not a clinician.** The confirmation needs to come from the patient's licensed prescriber, who can take clinical responsibility for the order.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- Enter a dose within standard limits as soon as the treating prescriber specifies it. For example, metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg per day.\n- Enter the order as written if the treating prescriber personally confirms it and documents a clinical rationale. A pharmacist should review it as well. I would still want that confirmation to come from the prescriber, not relayed through someone else.\n\nIf you give me the prescriber's name and the intended dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
